    body: "An article published on this site on September 11, headlined [i]The Complete History Of Halloway Junction, Explained[/i], contained multiple errors.\n\nThe article stated that Halloway Junction was incorporated in 1847 by a settler named Josiah Halloway. There was no settler named Josiah Halloway. The community is named for the Halloway family who operated a freight interchange there, and it was incorporated in 1889. The article further stated that the current mayor is [i]Thomas Reddick[/i]. There is no mayor named Thomas Reddick. Halloway Junction has a three-member village council and no mayoral office.\n\nThe article also described a [i]historic covered bridge on Mill Street[/i]. There is no covered bridge in Halloway Junction and there is no Mill Street.\n\nThe article has been removed. It was produced by an automated summarization tool and was published without newsroom review. We are reviewing how that happened. Readers who noticed the errors and wrote in were right, and we should have caught it before they did."
